1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,890
Before buying another shirt, compare
it with one you already own.

2
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:06,535
Meet Threadroom.

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:11,485
A linen shirt costs sixty-eight dollars.

4
00:00:11,505 --> 00:00:14,335
The navy overshirt is already owned.

5
00:00:14,355 --> 00:00:18,920
Threadroom puts them in the same
fitting room, before another purchase.

6
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:23,595
Start with the original
sample and two garments.

7
00:00:23,615 --> 00:00:27,215
The interface asks permission to
send the selected photos to YouCam

8
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,930
for this try-on.

9
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:35,470
These two results came from
actual YouCam API tasks.

10
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:39,085
The linen shirt and navy overshirt
are generated visualizations of the

11
00:00:39,105 --> 00:00:44,100
same sample person. They are
not preloaded try-on results.

12
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:49,400
Before and after keeps the original in view.

13
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:52,730
Look at the linen shirt against that
reference, with the difference

14
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:55,160
in appearance easy to inspect.

15
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:03,310
Switch to the owned navy overshirt
and use the same reference.

16
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:07,405
A familiar piece gets equal attention,
instead of disappearing behind the

17
00:01:07,425 --> 00:01:09,390
idea of something new.

18
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:15,525
Save the comparison while
you weigh your options.

19
00:01:15,545 --> 00:01:20,035
This is the actual downloaded card,
carrying both looks, their labels

20
00:01:20,055 --> 00:01:24,535
and ownership status, plus a reminder
that visualization cannot verify

21
00:01:24,555 --> 00:01:26,120
physical fit.

22
00:01:27,250 --> 00:01:29,650
Then make the assumption your own.

23
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:34,400
At fifty estimated wears, sixty-eight
dollars becomes one dollar and thirty-six

24
00:01:34,420 --> 00:01:38,640
cents per wear. The number changes
with your estimate, not an

25
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,350
AI prediction.

26
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:48,665
The same workspace is available in English,
Traditional Chinese, and Japanese.

27
00:01:48,685 --> 00:01:52,625
The results stay available as the
interface changes, rather than starting

28
00:01:52,645 --> 00:01:54,455
another generation.

29
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:57,555
Photos deserve a boundary.

30
00:01:57,575 --> 00:02:02,010
The privacy panel explains third-party
processing and retention.

31
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:04,915
Sharing your card remains your choice.

32
00:02:04,935 --> 00:02:09,365
Local controls cannot promise deletion
from the provider's systems.

33
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:12,960
Threadroom leaves the decision with you.

34
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:17,135
Something new, something already yours,
and a little more thought before

35
00:02:17,155 --> 00:02:18,905
the next purchase.
